      <SummaryInformationList count="1">
        <SummaryInformation id="63385" lang="en">
          <TextSectionList count="1">
            <TextSection id="83697" lang="en">
              <TextSectionType id="16907">
                <Name lang="en">Definition</Name>
              </TextSectionType>
              <Contents>A rare primary bone dysplasia characterized by the association of multiple epiphyseal dysplasia with macrocephaly and dysmorphic facial features (such as frontal bossing, hypertelorism, flat malar region, low-set ears, and short neck). Patients are of normal stature and present with joint swelling and &lt;i&gt;genu valgum&lt;/i&gt;. Additional reported manifestations include clinodactyly, spindle-shaped fingers, and &lt;i&gt;pectus excavatum&lt;/i&gt;.</Contents>
            </TextSection>
          </TextSectionList>
        </SummaryInformation>
      </SummaryInformationList>
    </Disorder>
